            <ArticleTitle>Infectious aneurysm of the two primary iliac arteries: rare localization of Salmonella typhimurium infection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>686-688</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1684/abc.2017.1294</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Infectious aneurysm is a severe entity of the aneurysmal pathology, due essentially to a bacterial agent. The most frequently implicated organisms are salmonella and staphylococci. We report the case of an infectious aneurysm of the two primitive iliac arteries with Salmonella typhimurium in a 70-year-old man.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
